# PropTrack Design System for Future AI Agents

This is the first file future AI agents should read before changing UI. The design system follows Gleap-inspired principles with a monochrome accent.

## Source of Truth

Read these files before making UI changes:

- `designsystem` - this guide
- `src/index.css` - global tokens, base components, tables, buttons, forms, badges
- `src/components/Layout/Layout.css` - sidebar, topbar, main content, mobile bottom nav
- `src/pages/Landing.css` - public landing page visual language
- `src/components/common/*.css` - reusable modal, slide panel, custom select, toggle styles

Do not use deleted or old references such as `design-system/property-tracking/MASTER.md` or `.agent/PROPERTY_SYSTEM.md`.

## Product Identity

PropTrack MY is an operational property portfolio management app. The UI should feel:

- Spacious and calm
- Dense where data demands it
- Fast and practical
- Premium but restrained
- Built for repeated dashboard work

Prefer scannable workflows, clear data hierarchy, and compact controls over decorative marketing composition.

## Visual Direction

The active visual direction is Gleap-inspired:

- Both light and dark themes available
- Warm tones (cream canvas in light, warm dark in dark theme)
- Inter typography for body, Playfair Display for editorial headlines
- Single monochrome accent (`var(--text-primary)`) for primary actions and interactivity
- Soft rounded containers (10px controls, 24px cards, 42px large elements)
- Subtle shadows, no heavy glassmorphism in light theme
- Semantic status colors only where they communicate state

Avoid: colorful SaaS gradients, teal real-estate branding, luxury editorial typography in body text, sharp corners.

